From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:30:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpu: vivante,gc: Allow up to four resets

Some SoCs split the reset of a core into one line per interface, for
example the core, the AXI and AHB interfaces and the on-chip memory of
the Allwinner A733 NPU. With its AXI and AHB resets asserted, that core
reads as model 0.

Allow up to four resets and describe them, the core reset first, so a
core with a single reset is unchanged.

Not covered: reset-names. The driver acts on all resets together and
does not need to tell them apart.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with a device tree that
uses this binding; the NPU node with four resets probes and dtbs_check
reports nothing.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/vivante,gc.yaml | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/vivante,gc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/vivante,gc.yaml
index b1b10ea70ad9..822a10d4f3f7 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/vivante,gc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/vivante,gc.yaml
@@ -44,7 +44,12 @@ properties:
     maxItems: 4
 
   resets:
-    maxItems: 1
+    items:
+      - description: GPU core reset
+      - description: AXI/master interface reset
+      - description: AHB/slave interface reset
+      - description: On-chip SRAM reset
+    minItems: 1
 
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
